                <pb facs="0790" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg696"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Office of the Treasurer of Exchequer</hi>.</placeName> [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1896-02-25T23:59:59-05:00"
                            notBefore="1896-02-01T00:00:00-05:29"
                    >undated</date>].</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">To the Owners of Estates, Republic of
                        Cuba:</hi></p>
                <p>Using the faculties conferred to me by the secretary of the exchequer, I hereby
                    notify the owners of estates that the only persons authorized to collect the
                    taxes are those designated by the Government, who should make themselves known
                    by showing their nomination papers, issued by the secretary of the treasury or
                    by the representative of the States of Las Villas.</p>
                <p>Please take note of above for your guidance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ernesto Fouts y Sterling</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">The Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
